 It's strange that someone posting from Intel would claim that productivity
gains are one-time. Hasn't Intel been increasing its productivity at a very
steady rate for the past couple of decades?
 You are right that I was inexcusably careless in my choice of numbers. I
expect something more like 50%/year to 100%/year until most of the mass in
the solar system becomes part of intelligent entities, at which time growth
will slow down except at the frontiers.

