Yes, the first person reading this hits the vote key(on a hypothetical
news/mail reader), selects "no informational content/off topic" from the
menu, and hits return.  When you go to read the article, your newsreader
indicates that the article has been voted to be trash by >n people you
trust, so it kills it from your view.  Since the voting procedure can
include other variables, such as "good post" "good opinion" "important
question", etc, you can discard bias on the part of a small number, or
perhaps even larger numbers, of the respondents whishing to censor a post
as long as a few mark it as good and you set your reader.

